Emerald 3DS changes to pret/pokeemerald 76463dac15cad36aca5e2b3f6366abf9e53f814f: Japanese names are native in Japanese builds
Applies after 0057-japanese-native-glyphs.patch; apply with tools/bootstrap.py.

The international code treats Japanese as the foreign script: GetBoxMonData wraps
Japanese nicknames in EXT_CTRL_CODE_JPN...ENG, ConvertInternationalString wraps names,
PadNameString pads the others so that they do not pass for Japanese ones, and so on.
In a Japanese build those names are native: IsForeignScriptLanguage (string_util.h)
is false there, as the Japanese ROM has no script switch and shows other games'
names as they are (wrapped, the Latin ones would not fit buffers sized for
5-character names). IsForeignGameLanguage keeps the Latin-script games out of the
Union Room and the trainer records, as the international games keep the Japanese
ones out. Link contests keep a Japanese partner's name as it came, and the battle
text keeps the wild/foe prefix in front of the name as the Japanese ROM does.
string_util.h includes constants/global.h for the language constants, as
mini_printf.c includes it without global.h. Other languages are unchanged.

diff --git a/include/string_util.h b/include/string_util.h
index 0a8a99f..3d92d83 100644
--- a/include/string_util.h
+++ b/include/string_util.h
@@ -1,6 +1,8 @@
 #ifndef GUARD_STRING_UTIL_H
 #define GUARD_STRING_UTIL_H
 
+#include "constants/global.h" // GAME_LANGUAGE and LANGUAGE_*: mini_printf.c has no global.h
+
 extern u8 gStringVar1[0x100];
 extern u8 gStringVar2[0x100];
 extern u8 gStringVar3[0x100];
@@ -43,4 +45,32 @@ s32 StringCompareWithoutExtCtrlCodes(const u8 *str1, const u8 *str2);
 void ConvertInternationalString(u8 *s, u8 language);
 void StripExtCtrlCodes(u8 *str);
 
+// Whether a name in this language is in the other script and converted to be shown:
+// the international games wrap Japanese names in EXT_CTRL_CODE_JPN/ENG and pad or
+// shorten them. Japanese is the Japanese game's own script and, like the Japanese
+// ROM (which has no script switch), it shows other games' names as they are:
+// wrapped, the longer Latin names would not fit buffers sized for 5-character
+// Japanese ones.
+static inline bool32 IsForeignScriptLanguage(u32 language)
+{
+#if GAME_LANGUAGE == LANGUAGE_JAPANESE
+    (void)language;
+    return FALSE;
+#else
+    return language == LANGUAGE_JAPANESE;
+#endif
+}
+
+// A linked game in the other script, which the Union Room and the trainer records
+// leave out: the Japanese games for an international one, the Latin-script games for
+// a Japanese one.
+static inline bool32 IsForeignGameLanguage(u32 language)
+{
+#if GAME_LANGUAGE == LANGUAGE_JAPANESE
+    return language != LANGUAGE_JAPANESE;
+#else
+    return language == LANGUAGE_JAPANESE;
+#endif
+}
+
 #endif // GUARD_STRING_UTIL_H
